--TEST--
`startProfile` under a mode naming `profile` and a granted path starts, a second start throws a `LogicError` until `stopProfile`, a stop with no profile running does nothing, and a stopped profile may start again — `rule:testing/debug-surface`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Debug::startProfile
// covers: Core\Debug::stopProfile
//
// Nothing writes the profile's file yet, so this case never reads it.
class Calc {
    public static function double(int $n): int {
        return $n * 2;
    }
}

// A stop with no profile running does nothing, and does not throw.
Core\Debug::stopProfile();
echo "stopped nothing\n";

Core\Debug::startProfile('./out/first.json');
echo "profile started\n";
try {
    Core\Debug::startProfile('./out/second.json');
    echo "second profile started\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
echo Calc::double(21), "\n";
Core\Debug::stopProfile();

// The stop closed the first profile, so the next start succeeds.
Core\Debug::startProfile('./out/second.json');
echo "profile started again\n";
Core\Debug::stopProfile();
Core\Debug::stopProfile();
echo "stopped twice\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[debug]
mode = ["profile"]

[capabilities.debug]
profile = ["./out"]
--FILE out/note.txt--
note
--EXPECT--
stopped nothing
profile started
Core\Debug::startProfile cannot start a profile, because one is already running. Call `Core\Debug::stopProfile` first.
42
profile started again
stopped twice
